#. Tag: title
#: kde-office.docbook:35
#, no-c-format
msgid "Office"
msgstr "Burèu"

#. Tag: title
#: kde-office.docbook:38
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction to KOffice"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-office.docbook:41
#, no-c-format
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &kde; project has also created a fully featured office suite called "
"&koffice; which adheres to standards and fits very well into the &kde; "
"desktop. This section was written with version 1.4 of &koffice; in mind."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:48
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&koffice; is a highly integrated office suite that builds directly on the "
"KDE technology. This has many advantages in terms of integration, features, "
"performance, familiar look and feel and so on. All technologies like &DCOP;, "
"KIO, KParts are directly available."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In particular the KParts technology is extended for the &koffice; components "
"to allow very flexible embedding of documents inside documents."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Because much technology is already present inside &kde; itself, &koffice; is "
"a very lightweight office suite, which results in fast application startup "
"and low memory consumption. This makes &koffice; a very suitable office "
"suite for older hardware as well, which can save lots of costs in some cases."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&koffice; is also a very feature complete office suite. It is not limited to "
"word processing, spreadsheets or presentations, but has also components for "
"image manipulation, flow charts, business report generation, database "
"management and project management. Because of the flexible component "
"integration smaller utilities like the diagram and chart engine as well as "
"the formula editor are available as stand alone tools."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As you can see &koffice; brings a lot of features that can enrich your "
"office experience. Its straight forward and &kde; like approach in look and "
"feel as well as familiar usability makes &koffice; quite useful for daily "
"office work."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-office.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid "Features"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This list gives a general outline of the &koffice; features. The &koffice; "
"office suite is too large to list every detail."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-office.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid "&koffice; features:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Fully builds on &kde; which makes these technologies available at low costs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid "Fully integrates into &kde; which is vital for business environments."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kde; technologies include document location abstraction, DCOP scripting, "
"parts and plugins,..."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid "Full Component embedding."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid "Low memory footprint, fast startup, lightweight."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid "Feature complete: many components are offered."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:101
#, no-c-format
msgid "Intuitive, good looking and easy to learn user interface."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adheres to standards: OASIS OpenDocument file format."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-office.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid "OASIS OpenDocument file format"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is important for an office suite to use standards where possible, "
"especially for the file format. The OASIS OpenDocument file format "
"specification is an open standard for office applications. This format is "
"spreading more and more, it is also the same file format OpenOffice.org "
"uses, which means that file exchange with any user of this office suite is "
"easily possible."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Adhering to official standards is always a good thing. For business "
"environments it is even vital to exactly know about their documents."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&koffice; has more components to offer than what is covered by the OASIS "
"specification. Still, all components covered by the specifications actually "
"use the OASIS OpenDocument file format."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-office.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid "&koffice; Components Overview"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:146
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Keep in mind that all these components can integrate very well into each "
"other. So basically a spreadsheet can contain anything from charts to "
"presentations, reports and even text documents. Likewise almost any "
"component can contain almost any other."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-office.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kword;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:152
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The textprocessing component, but it includes many aspects of a desktop "
"publishing application. This creates a rather unique mixture of features "
"that makes interesting layouts easily possible."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Website: <ulink url=\"http://www.koffice.org/kword/\">http://www.koffice.org/"
"kword/</ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: ulink
#: kde-office.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kword; Handbook"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-office.docbook:163
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kspread;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:164
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The spreadsheet component. &kspread; is a scriptable spreadsheet program "
"which provides both table-oriented sheets and support for complex "
"mathematical formulas and statistics. Features include Hyperlinks, cell data "
"validity checking with configurable warnings/actions, scripting and specific "
"cell customization."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:167
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Website: <ulink url=\"http://www.koffice.org/kspread/\">http://www.koffice."
"org/kspread/</ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: ulink
#: kde-office.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kspread; Handbook"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-office.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kpresenter;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:176
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The presentation component. It can be used to create on-screen presentations "
"or to design and print transparencies. Features include embedding images and "
"clip-art, easy working with objects, and the ability to make &HTML; or &XML; "
"slideshows."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:179
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Website: <ulink url=\"http://www.koffice.org/kpresenter/\">http://www."
"koffice.org/kpresenter/</ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: ulink
#: kde-office.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kpresenter; Handbook"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-office.docbook:187
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kivio;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The flowcharting and diagramming component. Additional stencil sets can be "
"used for custom needs, there is a plugin framework for additional "
"functionality, and even <acronym>UML</acronym> diagrams are possible."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:191
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Website: <ulink url=\"http://www.koffice.org/kivio/\">http://www.koffice.org/"
"kivio/</ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: ulink
#: kde-office.docbook:192
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kivio; Handbook"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-office.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid "&karbon14;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid "A vector-drawing application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-office.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid "&krita;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:205
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The painting and image manipulation component. &krita; contains both ease-of-"
"use, fun features like guided painting, as well as high-end features like "
"support for 16-bit images, <acronym>CMYK</acronym> and even OpenEXR "
"<acronym>HDR</acronym> images."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:208
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Website: <ulink url=\"http://www.koffice.org/krita/\">http://www.koffice.org/"
"krita/</ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: ulink
#: kde-office.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid "&krita; Handbook"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-office.docbook:216
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kugar;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:217
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The appropriate component for creating business reports, which is "
"accomplished with an advanced designer that it has. Features include report "
"printing in postscript, full control of fonts, colors, text alignment and "
"wrapping, as well as open report definition files (with the layout stored as "
"&XML;)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:220
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Website: <ulink url=\"http://www.koffice.org/kugar/\">http://www.koffice.org/"
"kugar/</ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: ulink
#: kde-office.docbook:221
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kugar; Handbook"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: application
#: kde-office.docbook:228
#, no-c-format
msgid "KPlato"
msgstr "KPlato"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The component for project management, allowing for the planning and "
"scheduling of various projects."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:232
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Website: <ulink url=\"http://www.koffice.org/kplato/\">http://www.koffice."
"org/kplato/</ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-office.docbook:239
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kexi;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:240
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The data management component. It can be used for creating database schemas, "
"inserting data, performing queries, and processing data. Forms can be "
"created to provide a custom interface to your data. All database objects -- "
"tables, queries and forms -- are stored in the database, making it easy to "
"share data and database design."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:243
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Website: <ulink url=\"http://www.koffice.org/kexi/\">http://www.koffice.org/"
"kexi/</ulink> and <ulink url=\"http://kexi-project.org\">http://kexi-project."
"org</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: ulink
#: kde-office.docbook:244
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kexi; Handbook"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-office.docbook:251
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kchart;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:252
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The chart drawing component; it is used to embed charts into one of the "
"other &koffice; components. It's easy to use, highly customizable allowing "
"all of the parameters to be changed, and has a flexible layout."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:255
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Website: <ulink url=\"http://www.koffice.org/kchart/\">http://www.koffice."
"org/kchart/</ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: ulink
#: kde-office.docbook:256
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kchart; Handbook"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-office.docbook:263
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kformula;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:264
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A formula editor which provides the basic input facilities and support "
"functionality that appears in other &koffice; applications. Some of its "
"features include intelligent cursor management, multi-level undo support and "
"advanced syntax highlighting."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:267
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Website: <ulink url=\"http://www.koffice.org/kformula/\">http://www.koffice."
"org/kformula/</ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: ulink
#: kde-office.docbook:268
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kformula; Handbook"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-office.docbook:277
#, no-c-format
msgid "Related Information"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:278
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Main website: <ulink url=\"http://www.koffice.org\">http://www.koffice.org</"
"ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: ulink
#: kde-office.docbook:279
#, no-c-format
msgid "&koffice; Handbook"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-office.docbook:286
#, no-c-format
msgid "Further Information"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-office.docbook:288
#, no-c-format
msgid "Application Manuals"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:289
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each Koffice component comes with its own manual. These manuals offer all "
"the latest information about the various components &koffice; has to offer "
"and should be read to learn more about &koffice;. The application manuals "
"can be accessed by using the documentation KIO Slave in &konqueror; (that "
"is, typing <userinput>help:/<replaceable>application</replaceable></"
"userinput> into the Location toolbar) or by selecting the respective "
"handbook from the &khelpcenter;. The website is also a good place to find "
"out more; it is at <ulink url=\"http://www.koffice.org\">http://www.koffice."
"org</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-office.docbook:297
#, no-c-format
msgid "Internet Resources"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:298
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The primary site on the internet is <ulink url=\"http://www.koffice.org"
"\">http://www.koffice.org</ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:300
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You will also find information about the user and developer mailing lists as "
"well as additional developer resources."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:302
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Kexi project has even an additional website, which can be found at "
"<ulink url=\"http://www.kexi-project.org\">http://www.kexi-project.org </"
"ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-office.docbook:308
#, no-c-format
msgid "Plugin development"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-office.docbook:309
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&koffice; can easily be extended with plugins. Plugin development is not "
"very difficult and can be used to optimize your everyday workflow. Such "
"capabilities are probably very interesting in business environments to make "
"&koffice; meet individual requirements. You can either take a look at "
"existing plugins or read a general introduction at <ulink url=\"http://"
"developer.kde.org/documentation/tutorials/developing-a-plugin-structure/"
"index.html\"> the developer's site</ulink>. The general KDE developers "
"website is available at <ulink url=\"http://developer.kde.org/\">http://"
"developer.kde.org</ulink>."
msgstr ""
